ss=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1553577-why-a-cult-need-a-mummy#post1553577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty obvious why an Arisen need a cult. But why a cult need an Arisen?<br /> <br /> How a mummy's brutal raw power can bring prestige or wealth to a group of mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the ability to Call for a Sekhem 10 mummy to arise with a compulsion to solve a cult s problem is the main benefit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-01T11:15:51-07:00","id":1553580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1553577-why-a-cult-need-a-mummy#post1553577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty obvious why an Arisen need a cult. But why a cult need an Arisen?<br /> <br /> How a mummy's brutal raw power can bring prestige or wealth to a group of mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>In game mechanical terms, by analogy to the more conventional Mystery Cult Initiation rules, a Scorpion Cult's mummy's remains serve as the grounding relic of its faith in the absence of a dot-rated vessel to fill that role (which it does under the auspices of the Lifeweb of the mummy's Tomb), to go along with the purpose for which its serves its Judge and the doctrine (and, to a more prominent degree, Doctrines) that it adheres to.<br /> <br /> The cult needs a mummy because the mummy is the direct servant of the being whose dictates it serves and the mummy therefore is the symbol of their divine mandate, drawn together by the force of destiny that called its founders together. Without a mummy, a Scorpion Cult is just a bunch of random yahoos collecting artifacts and meddling with society according to a code of conduct; the stewardship over the remains of what can probably be termed at least a lesser culture-hero of a bygone age makes their mission <i>real</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}